From the properties of a sine curve, the displacement graph has:

\begin{itemize}
\item points of inflexion at: $x=0,\ \dfrac{\pi}{2},\ \pi,\ \dfrac{3\pi}{2},\ 2\pi$
\item minimum turning points at: $x=\dfrac{\pi}{4},\ \dfrac{5\pi}{4}$
\end{itemize}

\exfigure{1286_q32_s2}

Hence the displacement of the particle is increasing at an increasing rate when $\dfrac{\pi}{4}<x<\dfrac{\pi}{2}$ and $\dfrac{5\pi}{4}<x<\dfrac{3\pi}{2}$.
